Z||000000||artherd||08-06-2001||06:40 AM||||Hi Cliff, I'm sure you just need more things to work on for PFF, us paying you so liberally and all, so I thought I'd suggest a "low bandwidth" preference for the fourm :P)<P>It would require running images through a utility like imagemagik on the server, and reseting ALL image links (be they to fiero.nl or elsewhere.)  Not terribly difficult to accomplish, but it would increase your traffic somewhat (but maybe offset by the gains on fiero.nl images?)<P>In any event, server CPU and memory utilization will skyrocket, what kind of hardware are you running now, and what are the loads?<P>I have access to some powerful servers in the 'states that could maybe accomplish this resizing task on their own, and the only changes you'd need to make would be the profile thing, and a redirect to the US server that would then do the actual processing.<P>Let me know, I have a full T1 link, so images are literally almost instant at any size.  We are all not so fortunate, and in my web designs I try to adhere to this covenant "Thou shalt not create homepages loading longer than ten seconds at 28.8!!!)"<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
